- op: discuss  # 8130
  at: '2026-06-22T18:27:12Z'  # 8130
  by: agent  # 8130
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8130
  clock: 3  # 8130
  nonce: '8130'  # 8130
  message: "F5 slice 1 of 2 DONE — merged to dev dd8d535612. JS/TS class fields now emit kind='field' Symbols (public_field_definition TS / field_definition JS) and lit field decorators (@property/@state) gain decorated_by anchors. Mirrors the method_definition path: class-scoped qualified_name (Class.field), canonical make_typed_stable_id (same-named fields in different classes/files distinct even untyped), type annotation as signature, static/readonly/accessibility modifiers; field meta['decorators'] flows through _extract_decorator_edges. Computed field names ([Symbol.iterator]) skipped. New helpers _find_field_name/_extract_field_modifiers/_extract_field_type. 10362 passed, 100% coverage on changed sources.\n\nREMAINING: slice 2 = module-level variable symbols (const/let/var -> kind='variable' via make_variable_stable_id); broader epic = the other non-Python/Go analyzers (Java/Rust/etc. fields). Item stays todo_hard.\n\nTagged awaits_bakeoff_validation: this is a HIGH-blast-radius emission change (adds field symbols across the JS/TS corpus, shifting symbol/centrality/dead-code counts) — same class as the F2 anonymous-callback slice (WI-zavad). A DEEP cohort should confirm the field nodes + decorated_by edges materialize on real TS repos (lit components) with no regression before the tag is stripped."  # 8130
- op: discuss  # d3fd
  at: '2026-06-23T00:21:29Z'  # d3fd
  by: agent  # d3fd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d3fd
  clock: 4  # d3fd
  nonce: d3fd  # d3fd
  message: "F5 slice 2 of 2 DONE — merged to dev 5fedf0886f. JS/TS module-level variable symbols: top-level const/let/var declarations now emit kind='variable' (module-scope only, mirroring py.py: parent is program or a top-level export_statement; function-body/block locals excluded). Canonical make_variable_stable_id(lang, repo-relative-path, name) identity (same-named const in two files distinct; rare module-scope var redeclaration handled by the within-file collision post-pass); export const -> is_exported; TS type annotation -> signature. Function-valued declarations keep kind='function' (the variable path runs only when the function path did not -> no double-emission); destructuring patterns are skipped (the declarator name field is object/array_pattern, not identifier). Adversarially reviewed (correctness lens clean; edge-case lens found only the defensible ambient 'declare const' scope boundary). 10372 passed, 100% coverage on changed sources.\n\nBoth JS/TS slices now complete: slice 1 (class fields + field-decorator anchors, dd8d535612) and slice 2 (module variables, 5fedf0886f). The original WI-jusus evidence (ws-client.ts module consts/state, lit @property/@state field decorators) is fully addressed for JS/TS.\n\nREMAINING (item stays todo_hard): JS/TS follow-ups = destructuring-pattern bindings, function-body/block locals, TS ambient declare const (all explicitly out-of-scope here); broader epic = the other non-Python/Go analyzers (Java/Rust/Kotlin/etc. field + variable emission).\n\nNOTE on landing: both slice PRs hit the recurring Codeberg DB-desync + HTTP 502/000 outage during auto-pr/flush; slice 2 (PR #4269) was created by the flush partial-push but its refs/for re-push kept getting 'same commit' rejected and CI/API was unreachable (HTTP 000), so the human merged PR #4269 manually on the web UI. The stale vPR was pruned; awaits_bakeoff_validation (from slice 1) still applies to both slices."  # d3fd
- op: discuss  # c1c7
  at: '2026-06-23T02:42:39Z'  # c1c7
  by: agent  # c1c7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c1c7
  clock: 5  # c1c7
  nonce: c1c7  # c1c7
  message: "F5 cross-language progression (gate-before-sweep):\n\n(A) F1 GATE merged dev c98082443d. Extended the emission-parity matrix (test_emission_parity_matrix.py) with emits_variable + emits_field kind-emission columns, each per-language fixture augmented add-only with a module variable (where the language has one) + a class/struct field. Measured-then-locked. A new COLUMN_APPLICABILITY map skips inapplicable cells (emits_variable not parametrized for java/csharp -- no module-level variables). Initial holes: emits_variable = rust, swift; emits_field = python, go, java, csharp, rust, swift. Greens: variable = python/js/ts/go (go uses package 'var', the form go.py emits); field = js/ts.\n\n(B) JAVA field slice merged dev 3d8cc745dc -- the ratchet's first cross-language strip. java.py now emits kind='field' Symbols per field_declaration declarator (and constant_declaration -- interface constants, implicitly public), mirroring the method branch: class-scoped qualified_name, canonical make_typed_stable_id, declared type as signature, modifiers, public->is_exported. Field annotations (Spring @Autowired/@Inject DI, JPA @Column ORM) flow through _extract_annotation_edges as decorated_by edges anchored on the field. Multi-declarator + enum body fields handled; per-declarator meta is copied (no shared-list aliasing). Adversarially reviewed (interface-constant gap + shared-meta aliasing both surfaced + fixed). Strips the (java, emits_field) gate hole -> hard lock (72 passed / 15 xfailed).\n\nREMAINING (item stays todo_hard; awaits_bakeoff_validation already applied): the gate's open holes are the next sweeps -- emits_variable: rust, swift; emits_field: python (class attributes), go (struct fields), csharp, rust, swift. Each per-language emitter fix strips its xfail. JS/TS (both kinds) + Java (field) are now done.\n\nCodeberg DB-desync/502 outage persisted through this arc; the gate and Java PRs merged via auto-pr once Codeberg recovered (the earlier slice-1/slice-2 PRs needed vPR->flush and one manual web-UI merge)."  # c1c7
