  message: "F5 Go struct-field slice merged dev 4e885252d3 — the gate ratchet's SECOND cross-language strip (after Java). go.py now emits kind='field' Symbols per NAMED struct field (embeddings stay base_classes; multi-name 'a, b int' -> one per name), mirroring the func/method path: struct-scoped qualified_name, canonical make_typed_stable_id, declared type as signature, capitalization-derived is_exported. Strips the (go, emits_field) gate hole -> hard lock (80 passed / 14 xfailed on the matrix). go already emitted package vars, so the go row is now fully green (variable + field).\n\nGATE HOLES REMAINING (the per-language sweep queue; item stays todo_hard, awaits_bakeoff_validation applied): emits_field = python (class attributes), csharp, rust, swift; emits_variable = rust, swift. Done so far: JS/TS (both kinds), Java (field), Go (field). Each remaining per-language emitter fix strips its xfail."  # d6d8
