  nonce: '1475'  # 1475
  message: "F5 Swift slice merged dev 2c821f17ad — second DOUBLE strip. swift.py now emits kind='field' for stored properties inside a type body and kind='variable' for top-level let/var (both are bare property_declaration; the enclosing type discriminates via _get_enclosing_type, top-level via parent==source_file; fn-/closure-locals excluded). Computed properties stay kind='property'. Canonical make_typed_stable_id, type annotation as signature, public/open->is_exported. Strips (swift, emits_field) AND (swift, emits_variable) -> hard locks (86 passed / 9 xfailed). Swift was the LAST emits_variable hole, so EVERY emits_variable cell in the gate is now a hard lock.\n\nGATE STATUS: only ONE F5 hole remains — (python, emits_field) = python class-attribute field emission (python already emits module-level variables). Doing it next CLOSES the F5 cross-language gate entirely (every cell a hard lock). Done so far: JS/TS (both), Java/Go/C# (field), Rust/Swift (field+variable)."  # 1475
